<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kuomboka</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kuomboka ('to get out of the water') is the annual ceremony of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lozi-people">Lozi</a> of western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zambia">Zambia</a>, held near the end of the rainy season when the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zambezi">Zambezi</a> floods the Bulozi plain. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/litunga">Litunga</a> travels in the royal barge <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nalikwanda">Nalikwanda</a>, paddled by dozens of men to the sound of royal drums, from his floodplain capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lealui">Lealui</a> to his dry-season residence at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/limulunga">Limulunga</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kuomboka.jpg" alt="Kuomboka" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Dietmar Hatzenbichler · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nalikwanda.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
